     "text": "{\"cost\": 10, \"rationale\": \"Every exfiltration technique requires admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold there, which requires reach_internal plus stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin only comes from admin_dc or admin_adfs. Each of those needs a foothold there plus stolen_admin. stolen_admin only comes from kerberoasting, which needs a foothold on the appserver or apiserver. That foothold in turn needs reach_internal and stolen_user. A minimal chain is: phish_workstation (gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user), pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc, auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db, exfiltrate_db. That is 10 techniques, and none can be removed because each step satisfies a requirement that nothing else provides more cheaply.\"}"
